  "rules": "Three merchants sit in fixed order A (seat 1), B (seat 2), C (seat 3). Each starts with {starting_florins} florins (public), a ship with room for {ship_capacity} cards, and three public commodity tracks (Spice, Silk, Grain) at {track_start}. The three commodities are shuffled and one is dealt secretly to each player as their Patron: every player has a different Patron and knows only their own.\n\nThe deck has {deck_size} cards: for each of Spice, Silk and Grain there are {cards_per_commodity} cards valued 0, 1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 4, 4, 5.\n\nSTART OF EACH DAY. There are {days} days. All {deck_size} cards are shuffled into a face-down deck and every ship is emptied (tracks are NOT reset). The top {dock_size} cards are turned face up in a row: the Dock, ordered first, second, third. The first active player is A on day 1, B on day 2 and C on day 3; the active role then passes in seat order A, B, C, A... each round. Each day has exactly {rounds_per_day} rounds.\n\nEACH ROUND. (1) The Dock, all ships, tracks and florins are announced. (2) The active player chooses a lot size of {min_lot_size} to {max_lot_size} (no more than the cards in the Dock). The lot is the first that many Dock cards; its size is its card count and its value is the sum of its card values. (3) Auction, once around: the next player in seat order after the active player bids first, then the other non-active player, then the active player last. Each bidder either passes (0) or bids a whole number that is at least {min_bid}, higher than the current highest bid, and no more than their florins. A player whose ship lacks room for the whole lot, or whose florins do not exceed the current highest bid, must pass. (4) If anyone bid, the highest bidder pays that many florins to the bank and loads every card of the lot onto their ship; for each card loaded, that player's track in the card's commodity rises by 1, to a maximum of {track_max}. If everyone passed, the lot is discarded and no florins, ships or tracks change. (5) The lot's cards leave the Dock, the remaining Dock cards slide forward in order, and the Dock is refilled to {dock_size} cards from the deck (fewer if the deck runs out).\n\nEND OF DAY (after round {rounds_per_day}). (a) Ship scoring: players are ranked by the total value of the cards on their ship. The highest gets {ship_prize_first} florins and the second gets {ship_prize_second}. Tied players add the prizes for the places they occupy and split them equally, rounded down. A player with an empty ship gets nothing. (b) Commodity majorities: for each commodity, the player with the highest track gets {majority_prize_first} florins and the second highest gets {majority_prize_second}. Ties split as above. A track at 0 earns nothing. (c) Patron: a player who earned a majority award in step (b) in their own Patron commodity receives that same amount again; a player who earned nothing there gets no bonus. All awards are added to florins.\n\nEND OF GAME. After day {days} scoring, Patrons are revealed and the player with the most florins wins. Players tied for the most share the win (a draw)."
